<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ningthouja dynasty</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ningthouja dynasty, of the Mangang clan of the Meitei, ruled Manipur from the founding traditionally dated to 33 CE until the kingdom merged with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> in 1949. Its kings, starting with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nongda-lairen-pakhangba">Nongda Lairen Pakhangba</a>, gradually brought the other Meitei clans of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imphal">Imphal</a> valley under their rule. The royal chronicle, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cheitharol-kumbaba">Cheitharol Kumbaba</a>, records their reigns.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ningthouja-dynasty.jpg" alt="Ningthouja dynasty" width="297" height="340" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Cookie at Spanish Wikipedia · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:In-29manipur.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
